# Monthly Table Maintenance Review Memo

Audit date: 2026-09-01. Size class is computed from total_pages only (>=500 large, <500 small), ignoring the legacy size_class column including medium traps. Bloat ratio is computed as dead_pages / total_pages with round-half-up to 2 decimal places. A ratio exactly equal to the applicable cap is compliant because the policy flags only ratios strictly over the cap; when stats are stale, the effective tightened cap governs the comparison.

## Non-compliant findings

- T-82 is STALE_STATISTICS, computed size_class large from total_pages 1000, dead_pages 80 and total_pages 1000 give computed round-half-up ratio 0.08, stats are stale at 55 days, which tightened cap to 0.10; legacy days_since_analyze field ignored, ratio does not exceed the cap.
- T-13 is AUTOVACUUM_DISABLED, computed size_class large from total_pages 1000, legacy small ignored, dead_pages 500 and total_pages 1000 give computed round-half-up ratio 0.50, stats are stale at 50 days, which tightened cap to 0.10; legacy days_since_analyze field ignored, autovacuum_enabled is False, so autovacuum is disabled.
- T-17 is AUTOVACUUM_DISABLED, computed size_class large from total_pages 1000, legacy small ignored, dead_pages 400 and total_pages 1000 give computed round-half-up ratio 0.40, stats are stale at 50 days, which tightened cap to 0.10; legacy days_since_analyze field ignored, autovacuum_enabled is False, so autovacuum is disabled.
- T-72 is AUTOVACUUM_DISABLED, computed size_class large from total_pages 1000, dead_pages 400 and total_pages 1000 give computed round-half-up ratio 0.40, stats are stale at 50 days, which tightened cap to 0.10; legacy days_since_analyze field ignored, manual vacuum override disables autovacuum even though autovacuum_enabled is True.
